From bcad5a7c59982604166d3c2e9671fd7a7a6feb10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:19:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915: HDR10+ vendor InfoFrame over HDMI where the HDMI
 one says nothing

HDR10PLUS_VSIF (linux-9980) on i915 and xe, on the HDMI connectors of
display version 10 and later (those with HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA).

The transcoder has one DIP for a vendor InfoFrame. The HDR10+ InfoFrame
takes it only where the HDMI vendor InfoFrame carries nothing: no HDMI
VIC, no 3D. DRM signals 2160p24, 25 and 30 with the HDMI VIC there and
VIC 0 in the AVI InfoFrame (drm_mode_hdmi_vic()), the 1000/1001 rates
too. Those modes go out with their CTA VIC in the AVI InfoFrame instead
(93, 94, 95, and 98 for 4096x2160p24) and an HDMI vendor InfoFrame
without the HDMI VIC, as NVKMS signals them and as Amlogic sends HDR10+
next to them, so that the DIP can carry HDR10+, but only:
- to an HDMI 2.0 sink (SCDC) that lists that VIC in its video data block
  and declares HDR10+ in its EDID (application version 1 or later);
- in a configuration whose commit carries HDR10PLUS_VSIF, or in any
  commit of the same mode as the one on the screen when that one went
  out with the CTA VIC already, with ALLOW_MODESET or without: the end of
  HDR10+, the end of the video and the next video at that mode change
  nothing of the signalling, and the next change of mode signals the
  mode as DRM does again. A video thus takes one change of mode, as
  without HDR10+.
The rest of the AVI InfoFrame stays as DRM fills it. Anywhere else (SDR,
HDR10, a sink that does not fit, 3D) the mode goes out exactly as
before, and HDR10+ at it is refused: the kernel log says so once (user
space only learns that the commit failed). Never with the Dolby VSIF of
the tunnel, nor to a sink that takes no vendor InfoFrames.

A change of HDR10PLUS_VSIF is a fastset, as one of HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA
is: the comparison of the pipe configurations leaves the vendor
InfoFrame out of a fastset when either side sends HDR10+, and
intel_ddi_update_pipe_hdmi() writes the vendor DIP again where the new
state sends HDR10+ or the DIP holds it. The readout takes the HDR10+
InfoFrame back from the DIP (infoframes.hdr10plus), so that the state
checker compares it.

Not over DisplayPort: there the HDR10+ InfoFrame SDP is 33 bytes and
the free DIP (the vendor one) holds 32; the gamut metadata DIP carries
the HDR one.

Checked: W=1 without new warnings, i915 and xe compiled; host test of
the rule and of the DIP layout (intel_hdr10plus.h) with mutations; host
test of the CTA VIC with the kernel's own InfoFrame packer
(drivers/video/hdmi.c) and the EDIDs of an S90H, a G60SD and an LG C5,
the AVI and vendor InfoFrames byte by byte, today's bytes wherever the
CTA VIC does not apply, with mutations; intel_hdmi.c compiled with the
command of the kernel's build. Not run on a GPU.
